        <body>
            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="0997" n="897" xml:id="pg897"/>

                <head>No. 578.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Fairchild.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-06-15"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 15,
                        1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 30.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the 11th instant I received a call from
                    the Austro-Hungarian minister in Washington, during which he stated that his
                    government had instructed its representatives in the Morocco conference at
                    Madrid to endeavor to secure religious liberty and complete religious toleration
                    for all classes in Morocco, in accordance with the proposition of the Berlin
                    conference. I at once telegraphed you as follows: “Support the Austrian
                    proposition before conference to secure religious toleration in Morocco.”</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
